supply gaza's only power plant and  increase the availability of electricity  which was down to around eight hours a  day  ukraine and russia blaming each other  for the repeated shelling of europe's  largest nuclear power plant the zaparica  nuclear facility was captured by russian  forces back in march but it is still  being operated by ukrainian technicians  over the past few days the complex has  been hit several times by artillery and  rocket fire with both sides blaming each  other and warning of a potential nuclear  disaster if critical components are  damaged the u.n nuclear watchdog is  calling for utmost restraint the plant's  located just outside a russian-held city  with a population of more than 50 000  people  after a dangerous and difficult journey  through the black sea the first ship  carrying ukrainian grain has now docked  at a turkish port the polar net left  odessa friday carrying 12 000 tons of  corn after being trapped in port for  months during the voyage the ship had to  navigate a narrow passage through  minefields and undergo a series of  international inspections also today two  more grain ships left ukrainian ports  bringing the number of vessels sailing  under the u.n brokered safe passage deal  to 10.  fire crews are struggling to contain a  huge blaze at cuba's largest oil storage  facility  overnight a second oil tank at the  matanzas super tank port caught fire and  exploded fire has been spreading through  the facility since friday when it was  hit by lightning at least one  firefighter has been killed and 16  people are missing the fire is expected  to worsen cuba's ongoing fuel crisis the  port's located about 100 kilometers east  of havana  sharing the load ahead why one of the  world's biggest airlines is asking its  bosses to help with the bags  air travel this summer has been plagued  by lengthy delays just about everywhere  and canadian airlines and airports are  not immune to the pandemic fueled  staffing issues making for 